"""Chemistry Olympiad unit 16: the single steps that camp-level problems turn on.

Found by reading a mock USNCO Part II and a mock camp test (Anugrah Chemparathy's public collection) and mapping
each part to the objective that would answer it. Most problems had their first half in the Library and lost it at
one step; these are those steps, one question each. The collection is free for personal use only and this repo is
public, so nothing here is taken from it: no problem text, no data tables, no compounds chosen because a problem
used them beyond the textbook systems any course uses. The topics were the checklist; the items are ours.

Numeric items are recomputed along another route where one exists. Organic and descriptive inorganic items are
authored multiple choice, kept to standard textbook facts; stereodescriptors are not machine-checked.
"""
from opl_dsl import Q

FILE, FRAMEWORK, PRACTICE = "co-camp-steps", "chemistry-olympiad", "P1"
MC = ["{{o1}}", "{{o2}}", "{{o3}}", "{{o4}}"]
